cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Rule 16.1 Tracker: Initial Management Orders in Multidistrict Litigation Since December 1, 2025"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Luhmann"
    given-names: "Zach"
    affiliation: "New York University School of Law"
abstract: >-
  A complete, continuously updated record of how federal transferee courts have
  applied Fed. R. Civ. P. 16.1, the first MDL-specific Federal Rule, since it
  took effect on December 1, 2025. The universe is every MDL centralized by the
  Judicial Panel on Multidistrict Litigation on or after that date, taken from
  the Panel's own monthly report rather than from any search, so that MDLs whose
  orders never name the Rule are counted too. Sixteen MDLs are in the universe
  and fifteen have a readable initial management order; eight of those cite the
  Rule and seven do not. Each order is coded against 61 variables covering every
  enumerated topic in Rule 16.1(b)(2) and (b)(3), the threshold applications of
  16.1(a), (b)(1) and (c), and matters courts added beyond the Rule. Every cell
  carries a pin cite, and every cell on which direction or resolution is recorded
  carries a verbatim quotation. A companion table records party filings that
  invoke the Rule, including in proceedings outside 28 U.S.C. 1407. Codebook
  v1.1 followed a full independent recode and two-adjudicator review, in which
  22 of 300 cells were amended; fifteen contested cells remain open and are
  recorded as such. Known limitations are logged in AUDIT.md, which is part of
  the dataset rather than an appendix to it.
keywords:
  - multidistrict litigation
  - Federal Rules of Civil Procedure
  - Rule 16.1
  - case management
  - empirical legal studies
repository-code: "https://github.com/zachluhmann/rule-16-1-tracker"
url: "https://zachluhmann.github.io/rule-16-1-tracker/"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.1"
date-released: 2026-08-31
